# L §4.2 schedule(p, e, roll, cal): "A day that doesn't exist in p (31 February) gives none ... a move whose day is
# none has no instance at that key".  Day 31 of 2026-01..2026-03: instances on 2026-01-31 and 2026-03-31 only, so
# two movements of 100.00 PLN (200.00 PLN, L §5.14.3 flows of a move).
=== m.tally
model sch
  tally 2
  on 2026-01-01
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "umowa"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01
place konto: accounts PLN lives 2020-01-01..
place world: outside lives 1900-01-01..
index qm = month 2026-01..2026-03
input dom: int
input amt: money PLN
input cal: calendar

move pay[m in qm]: transfers
  on schedule(m, dom, unadjusted, cal)
  leg cash from konto to world amount amt

version v
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  dom = 31
  amt = 100.00 PLN
  cal = calendar(weekends [sat, sun])
  opening[konto] = 1 000.00 PLN at 2026-01-01 start

ask q1: count(x in transfers over 2026), flows(pay, 2026)
ask q2: x.day for x in transfers over 2026
=== expect
q1: (2, 200.00 PLN)
  cut 2026-01-01
q2 (x = pay[2026-01]): 2026-01-31
  cut 2026-01-01
q2 (x = pay[2026-03]): 2026-03-31
  cut 2026-01-01
